# Project Model

## Projects and workflows

- A **project** is a folder that can hold any work (ADR 0043), and it is the unit of access control. It may be a Git repository or a plain folder.
- A **workflow** has no id or table of its own. It is identified by `(projectId, workflowName)`, where `workflowName` is its exported name. Tables that reference workflows (`workflow_runs`, `workflow_enablements`, `trigger_definitions`) store `workflow_name`.
- Workflows are discovered by parsing source (`packages/parser`). There is no kind field, registry file, or manifest.

## Tenancy and identity

- The hierarchy is tenant, then project, then workflow. There is **no default tenant or user**. `tenantId` is the host's org id from its auth context on every request; the tenant row is upserted on first project create.
- Permissions follow ADR 0158: `thing:action` grants (`program:write`, `runs:read`, and so on) from role files, with no `builder` flag. Clients read effective permissions from `GET /me`.

## The `.catamorphic/` workspace (ADR 0142)

- Workflows, apps, contracts, scripts, project agents, roles, and skills live in `.catamorphic/`, an independent Bun workspace created on first capability use. Paths come from constants in `packages/parser/src/types.ts` (`PROJECT_WORKSPACE_ROOT`, `WORKFLOW_SOURCE_ROOT`, `APP_SOURCE_ROOT`, `CONTRACTS_SOURCE_ROOT`).
- Never write framework dependencies into the project's root manifest, and preserve root files and owner instructions.
- Project-owned mutable data lives in `.catamorphic/app-data/`, ignored by `.catamorphic/.gitignore`. Logical `store/...` document addresses map to `app-data/store/...`; a root `store/` is ordinary user content. Preserve owner edits to ignore rules.
- Profiles, credentials, caches, staging, and managed worktrees stay in host storage, never in the project.

## Git behavior

- **Opening an existing folder is inert** (ADR 0141): no Git init, manifest writes, seeds, installs, or copied history. Initialize Git only for an operation that needs history.
- New managed projects start with `.catamorphic/project.json`, scoped ignore rules, and host-selected seeds, with no root package manifest. GitHub import clones once and keeps history and the real default branch. New repositories default to `main`.
- Adopted local checkouts use native Git; portable managed working copies use isomorphic-git.
- Imported local work is committed and shared explicitly (ADR 0104). A settled agent turn alone never authorizes publishing imported work.
- Every Run executes an immutable deployment artifact or session artifact; `workflow_runs` records which. There is no run mode.

## Storage contracts

Two contracts in `packages/git/src/types.ts`:

- **`StorageBackend`** (working copies): `FsBackend` (a host-resolved project root folder, or `<basePath>/<tenantId>/<projectId>/dev/<externalUserId>/`) and `DaytonaBackend` (`@catamorphic/daytona`, experimental).
- **`RemoteBackend`** (bare origins): `FsRemoteBackend`, `ObjectRemoteBackend` over any object store (`S3ObjectStore` from `@catamorphic/s3`, ADR 0012), `ArtifactsRemoteBackend` (`@catamorphic/cloudflare`), and `CheckoutRemoteBackend` for attached local checkouts. Remote sync (`syncWithNetworkRemote`, ADR 0044) fetches, merges, pushes, and keeps rescue branches.

Working-copy file APIs reject absolute paths, `..`, and `.git` access. Remote backends isolate by tenant and project key and update refs with compare-and-swap.

## Database types

- Migrations are forward-only raw SQL in `packages/db/migrations/`, starting from the first-release baseline (ADR 0084). Tables live in the host-chosen schema (default `catamorphic`).
- After a migration, run `bun run db:migrate && bun run db:codegen`. Generated types land in `packages/db/src/generated/db.ts`; never edit them by hand.
- Query with Kysely and type rows as `Selectable<DB["table_name"]>`. Never duplicate row interfaces or cast rows.
- JSONB columns are `Json` / `JsonValue` from `@catamorphic/db` on the Kysely side and `z.unknown()` (nullable where the column is) in Zod, since JSONB can hold any JSON value, not only objects.
- UI code never imports `@catamorphic/db`; all data access goes through API routes.
